codex
The count-based formulation exposed a real limitation of the supplied semantics: `cntSub` is not declared total, so a symbolic comparison admits an undefined third branch even though single-character count is mathematically total. I’m switching to the semantics’ total character predicates (`isupper`/`islower`) and proving their loop with its own invariant; this removes the semantic definedness gap rather than axiomatizing it away.
apply patch
patch: completed
/work/solution.py
diff --git a/solution.py b/solution.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2cad906d0e0a178ae8f0a3930b34d4e8508aeb8a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/solution.py
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+def _extension_strength(extension):
+    score = 0
+    character = ""
+    for character in extension:
+        if character.isupper():
+            score += 1
+        if character.islower():
+            score -= 1
+    return score
+
+
+def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):
+    strongest = extensions[0]
+    strongest_strength = _extension_strength(strongest)
+    extension = strongest
+    score = strongest_strength
+    for extension in extensions:
+        score = _extension_strength(extension)
+        if score > strongest_strength:
+            strongest = extension
+            strongest_strength = score
+    return class_name + "." + strongest
